========================================================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================================================
INCONCLUSIVE (pre-registered): no on-disk cluster weak-lensing profile reaches 1.4 R500 (CLASH Tian+2020 rows stop at ~0.6 Mpc; X-COP on disk is hydrostatic X-ray, not shear). The [R500, 1.4 R500] window is under-powered by design: Delta_lnR = 0.336 vs 1.099, so the same stack reaches only ~1 sigma there (needs 46794 lenses vs 4316 for the full window); the ESD amplitude separation over the short window is 1.20x vs 2.03x. With the full [R500, 3 R500] window, a 4316-lens stack (bracket 1735-20204 for sigma_dex = 0.1-0.3, c = 3-5) separates the framework slope (-1.00, rho ~ r^-2) from the LambdaCDM NFW slope (-1.64) at 3 sigma.

